  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1234 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThe main upper level low will exit to the northeast towards Tuesday \nbut guidance does have lingering shortwave energy lingering behind \nthe system through Tuesday into Tuesday night. This and still the \npresence of some coastal troughing to the south looks to keep in \nsome low end pops (20-30%) across the area, favoring along and east \nof the I-35 corridor. Temperatures look to trend slightly milder \nthanks to any breaks that may occur within the clouds but it's now \nlooking more likely to be a struggle on getting any warmer than the \nupper 60s or low 70s across the region. \n\nLongwave troughing becomes entrenched from the Ohio Valley into the \nMississippi valley from Wednesday into Thursday. Shortwave energy \nadvancing southeastward from the Central plains into East Texas or \ninto the Texarkana region on the western periphery of the troughing \nlooks to help advance a weak cold front across our region sometime \nlate in the day on Wednesday into Wednesday night. The northwest \nflow behind this front helps to usher in some drier air and pushes \nany lingering rain chances in our eastern areas more to the \nsoutheast and out from our area by Wednesday night.\n\nThe end of the workweek into the start of the next weekend looks to \ntrend pleasant with returning ample sunshine and low humidity with \nno rain chances. The daytime highs trend seasonable in the low to \nmid 70s while overnight lows trend cooler, dipping ranging from mid \nto upper 40s into the low 50s.",
